## Implementation Approach

### 1. Start with Data Model

```typescript
// Define the core data structures first
interface User {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
  createdAt: Date;
}

// Database schema
const usersTable = pgTable('users', {
  id: uuid('id').primaryKey().defaultRandom(),
  email: varchar('email', { length: 255 }).notNullable().unique(),
  name: varchar('name', { length: 100 }).notNullable(),
  createdAt: timestamp('created_at').defaultNow(),
});
```

### 2. Build API Layer

```typescript
// API route with validation
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json();
  const validated = userSchema.parse(body);
  
  const user = await db.insert(usersTable).values(validated).returning();
  
  return Response.json({ success: true, user });
}
```

### 3. Create UI Components

```tsx
export function UserForm({ onSubmit }: UserFormProps) {
  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition();
  
  const handleSubmit = (formData: FormData) => {
    startTransition(async () => {
      await createUser(formData);
    });
  };
  
  return (
    <form action={handleSubmit}>
      <input name="email" type="email" required />
      <input name="name" type="text" required />
      <button type="submit" disabled={isPending}>
        {isPending ? 'Creating...' : 'Create User'}
      </button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

### 4. Wire Everything Together

- Connect components to APIs
- Handle loading and error states
- Add optimistic updates where appropriate
- Implement proper error boundaries

## Best Practices

### Code Organization
```
src/
├── app/           # Routes and pages
├── components/    # UI components
├── lib/           # Shared utilities
├── server/        # Server-only code
│   ├── db/        # Database layer
│   └── api/       # API handlers
└── types/         # TypeScript types
```

### Key Principles
- Type safety end-to-end
- Server components by default
- Validate at boundaries
- Handle all error states
- Test critical paths

